WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.070
In 2016, a group of truck makers
was fined 2.93 billion euros.

2
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.490
Their offence: agreeing prices with
each other instead of competing.

3
00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.460
A year later, Google was
fined 2.42 billion euros

4
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.380
for abusing its dominance
in online search.

5
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.980
So where should a government
draw the line between

6
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.540
tough competition and abuse?

7
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:27.790
In this mission, you'll sort the three kinds
of behaviour competition authorities target.

8
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.710
Then you'll break up a
cartel in a graph lab,

9
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.800
and measure what buyers gain.

10
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.410
Your mission: decide when a government
should step in to protect competition.
